<title>GERMANY: BHW SAYS SOLD DSL STAKE TO BANKS.</title>
<headline>BHW SAYS SOLD DSL STAKE TO BANKS.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German financial services group BHW Holding AG said on Tuesday it had sold its entire stake in Deutsche Siedlungs- und Landesrentenbank, DSL, to several German banks.</p>
<p>The group earlier said it had sold its remaining shares in state-controlled DSL, having last week reduced its holding in the bank to 10.5 percent from 20.69 percent.</p>
<p>There had been speculation, fuelled by recent consolidation in the German banking sector, that a single bank had bought up the holding.</p>
</text>
